sequenceDiagram
  participant A as Agent
  participant C as Coordinator / C6
  participant Q as PostgreSQL
  participant D as Donor
  participant P as Publisher / NAS
  A->>C: register (mTLS identity, session, version, source, storage)
  C->>Q: bind current session transactionally
  C-->>A: confirmed registration
  A->>C: heartbeat (resources / current attempt)
  C->>Q: confirm metrics and renew valid lease
  A->>C: lease (Idempotency-Key)
  C->>Q: lock worker / job / lazy chunk; new attempt
  Q-->>C: commit lease + stored response
  C-->>A: run / chunk / attempt / next_id / expiry / config
  loop Each actual redirect, retry or Range
    A->>C: request permit (UID, class, lease)
    C->>Q: validate authority / lease / session
    C-->>A: permit / epoch / connection lease
    A->>D: one actual HTTP request
    D-->>A: status / headers / body
    A->>C: release slot + feedback
    C->>Q: persist feedback and quota adaptation
  end
  A->>C: progress (body hash, sequence)
  C->>Q: confirm result / reserve space / advance only contiguous prefix
  A->>P: write own .part, fsync, SHA-256
  A->>C: commit stage / checksum / size / attempt
  C->>Q: publication verifying + stored 202
  C->>P: verify lease, copy to publisher-owned inode, hash, atomic rename
  C->>Q: transaction ready file + final result + checkpoint
  C-->>A: publication ready
  A->>C: repeat confirmed progress with same key/body
  C->>Q: read stored response
  C-->>A: previous result, no repeated side effects
